---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '../components/articles/ArticleHero.astro';
import ArticleContent from '../components/articles/ArticleContent.astro';
import ArticleStats from '../components/articles/ArticleStats.astro';
import ArticleContactForm from '../components/articles/ArticleContactForm.astro';
import ArticleTestimonials from '../components/articles/ArticleTestimonials.astro';
import ArticleMap from '../components/articles/ArticleMap.astro';

const title = "Contact Our Ann Arbor Personal Injury Lawyers | Free Consultation";
const description = "Contact Logeman & Iafrate for a free personal injury consultation. Call our Ann Arbor office or submit your case details online. We respond promptly.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <ArticleHero
    title="Contact Us"
    description="Personal injury attorney with three decades of experience fighting for injured clients in Michigan. He's known for compassionate and aggressive legal representation for injury victims."
    image="https://pagesmith-cdn.com/881ce63c/images/693497a35eaaff8688ef590f_relume-608351-1024.webp"
    imageSrcset="https://pagesmith-cdn.com/881ce63c/images/693497a35eaaff8688ef590f_relume-608351-640.webp 640w, https://pagesmith-cdn.com/881ce63c/images/693497a35eaaff8688ef590f_relume-608351-1024.webp 1024w"
    imageAlt="Lady Justice holding the scales of justice"
  />
  <ArticleContent>
    <h2>Supporting Your Recovery After Suffering A Catastrophic Injury</h2>

    <p>At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we recognize the immense challenges that come with recovering from catastrophic injuries. When you are focused on healing, dealing with legal battles is the last thing you need on your plate. Our dedicated team is here to shoulder your legal burdens, ensuring that you can concentrate on your recovery while we handle the complexities of your claim.</p>

    <p>With over 60 years of combined experience, Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., offers free consultations and operates on a no-win, no-fee basis. Our firm is known for taking on and winning cases that other attorneys might consider unwinnable. We are prepared to go to trial to secure the damages our clients need and deserve. Located in Ann Arbor, we serve clients across Michigan, providing you with the strong legal representation you need while you focus on your future.</p>

    <h2>The Devastating Impact Of Catastrophic Injuries</h2>

    <p>Catastrophic injuries are severe and can permanently alter your life. From expensive medical bills to permanent disabilities, you will likely deal with the impacts of these injuries for the rest of your life. These injuries require extensive medical treatment, continuous care, and can significantly impair your ability to work and perform daily activities. Fighting for fair compensation is the best way to secure your financial future and get the justice you deserve.</p>

    <p>Common types of catastrophic injuries include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Amputations and loss of limbs</li>
      <li>Paralysis, including paraplegia or quadriplegia</li>
      <li><strong>Spinal cord injuries</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Traumatic brain injuries</strong></li>
      <li>Severe burn injuries</li>
      <li>Multiple fractures</li>
    </ul>

    <p>At Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C., we have a strong reputation for advocating vigorously for our clients' best interests. We are committed to taking on challenging cases that other firms may shy away from, ensuring that our clients receive the justice and compensation they deserve. Whether your catastrophic injury occurred due to a <strong>car accident</strong> or a <strong>slip-and-fall</strong>, you can trust us to fight tirelessly for you.</p>

    <h2>What Are Considered Catastrophic Injuries?</h2>

    <p>Catastrophic injuries are those that result in permanent disabilities or long-term medical conditions. These injuries significantly disrupt the victim's lifestyle and ability to function independently. Catastrophic injuries can include spinal cord injuries, traumatic brain injuries, severe burns and amputations. These types of injuries not only cause intense physical pain and suffering but also emotional and financial distress.</p>

    <h2>How Do Catastrophic Injuries Affect Daily Life?</h2>

    <p>Catastrophic injuries can dramatically alter every aspect of daily life. Victims may face challenges such as loss of mobility, dependence on others for personal care and the inability to return to work, which can lead to significant financial strain. Victims may also experience feelings of helplessness, depression and anxiety about their future. The need for ongoing medical treatments and rehabilitation can make recovery a full-time endeavor, while adding a large strain on your family.</p>

    <h2>Can I Sue For Catastrophic Injuries Caused By Someone Else's Negligence?</h2>

    <p>If your catastrophic injuries were caused by someone else's negligence, you have the right to sue for compensation. This can include damages for medical expenses, lost wages, loss of future earning capacity, pain and suffering, and more. It is crucial to work with a skilled catastrophic injury attorney who can help prove the negligence of the other party and ensure that you receive the maximum compensation you are entitled to.</p>

    <h2>Get The Compensation You Need, Call Us Today</h2>

    <p>If you or a loved one has suffered catastrophic injuries due to someone else's negligence, do not hesitate to contact Logeman &amp; Iafrate, P.C. Call us at <a href="tel:+17349324622"><strong>(734) 994-0200</strong></a> or fill out our <strong>online contact form</strong> for a free consultation. We handle cases on a contingency-fee basis, meaning you owe us nothing unless we win your case. Let us help you secure the compensation you need to support your recovery and regain control over your life.</p>
  </ArticleContent>
  <ArticleStats />
  <ArticleContactForm />
  <ArticleTestimonials />
  <ArticleMap />
</BaseLayout>
